    "category": "Non-automatic weighing instrument",
    "type_designations": ["Checkmaster", "Linemaster V"],
    "module_designation": null,
    "description": "The instrument utilises the Checkmaster digital indicating device connected to a weighing platform to form a single-interval, Class III or IIII, non-automatic weighing instrument. The instrument is not intended to be used for direct sales to the public. Construction: stainless steel enclosure, LCD display, operator keypad with numerical, navigation and function keys, lightbar. Interfaces: load cell, 2 x RS232, 9 x PIO, Wi-Fi, RFID. Software is held in firmware on the circuit board with identification number MC8_xxx; a non-editable TAN (traceable access number) counter increments when legally relevant parameters are changed. Access to the load cell connection and electronics is prevented by sealing the enclosure using a wire and seal or a tamper-evident label and securing mark. Any compatible load cell(s) with a respective OIML R60 Certificate of Conformity may be used, subject to the compatibility of modules calculation."
